  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 104 AM EDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nMid to late week an upper level low moves into the eastern US and \nthen lingers off the New England coast through the weekend. A \nfrontal boundary will slide south across the state on Thursday and \nsettle either over far southern FL or across the Straits Friday and \nremain there through the upcoming weekend. Some drier air will \nlikely filter at least down to the lake region late in the week, but \nwill struggle to make it all the way through South FL. This is \nreflected in the PoPs for late in the week into the weekend with the \nhighest PoPs over the far southern peninsula and lower chance PoPs \nacross the northern half of the forecast area. Overall it will \nremain a wet and unsettled period across South FL, with at least \nisolated instances of urban flooding remaining possible each day. \n\nTemperatures through the extended period remain near normal with \nhighs each day generally in the upper 80s to lower 90s. Low \ntemperatures will be in the low to middle 70s.",
